    description:
      'The `data` payload for every mandate webhook event. Always contains the full `mandate`. Action events also carry the relevant sub-resource: `approval` on the three `approval_*` events, `revocation` on the three `revocation_*` events. The `created` and `canceled` events carry only the `mandate`.\n\n`mandate.status` reflects only the latest action. Read `mandate.canceledAt` and `mandate.revokedAt` to know what has durably happened: the on-chain spending allowance is gone precisely when `revokedAt` is set, and canceling alone does not remove it.',
